The audience is first-time, never-licensed Vermont applicants, typically teenagers on the learner's permit and junior license path and adults applying for a first driver's license, reading at a plain-English level with no assumed driving vocabulary. This section teaches how points attach to convictions, the point values of eight named offenses, the ten point suspension letter and hearing, the two year window that sets the suspension length, and the violations that carry no points. The content assumes no prior rule knowledge and no prerequisites beyond literacy; every term the section introduces is defined in the glossary lines of part C.
